        "abstract": "<jats:title>Abstract</jats:title><jats:p>We consider Artin's conjecture on primitive roots over a number field , reducing an algebraic number . Under the Generalised Riemann Hypothesis, there is a density  counting the proportion of the primes of  for which  is a primitive root. This density  is a rational multiple of an Artin constant  that depends on the largest integer  such that . The aim of this paper is bounding the ratio , under the assumption that . Over , this ratio is between  and 2, these bounds being optimal. For a general number field , we provide upper and lower bounds that only depend on .</jats:p>",
